 field induce a conserved scalar current in four-dimensional de Sitter space, including regimes without an asymptotic particle interpretation, and how does this current constrain inflationary magnetogenesis?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e8cc19c9a89ff281a022113db638ec13721d815971949b468b1de3aad633ab30","title":"Can the two abelian-containing polynomial candidates be completed into quantum gravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0019"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e8a506532850319212502f3f2f75b8bc3a1965f04745f06ac4b2fb348cfc331b","title":"Can self-reproducing inflation coexist with a finite effective-theory field range and a lower bound on the gradient of a positive scalar potential? The paper studies this compatibility conditionally, with explicit calculations for one slowly rolling inflaton.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0031"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e89e80dad9045810ca484e565e1086ef8ef61a8f30582d895c7751b4893e85ec","title":"Can positive-potential inflation satisfy the field-space restrictions conjectured for effective theories admitting quantum-gravity completion?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e85262ce9c3d2a946b5ea5b5d0185970761c7b66a72f424576895290e35cfc5c","title":"Which matter-field singularities contribute when a one-parameter GLSM sphere partition function is evaluated by contour integration?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0042"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e8c0a0bffd5b08931037fafc4f60b51a9c3f1973750a35405bcdcded2eaab51b","title":"Can axion inflation satisfy the assumed microscopic bound f < M_Pl while having an effective decay constant above M_Pl, through coher